Intel Graphics Compute Runtime (NEO) is the OpenCL and Level Zero
driver for Intel graphics hardware, including Intel Arc discrete
GPUs. It provides the runtime components needed to execute compute
workloads on Intel GPUs via OpenCL or the oneAPI Level Zero API.

Required dependencies: gmmlib, intel-graphics-compiler.

Optional dependencies not covered by this build:
  igsc: discrete GPU firmware enumeration via Level Zero
  libva: cl_intel_va_api_media_sharing OpenCL extension
  libdrm: cl_intel_va_api_media_sharing OpenCL extension

After installation, the OpenCL ICD is registered automatically
at /etc/OpenCL/vendors/intel.icd. No additional configuration
is required to use Intel GPU OpenCL.
